# Anything holding a secret, ahead of there being one to hold. The repository
# has none in any of its 144 commits and this is so that stays true: a stray
# .env is the one mistake a public repository cannot take back, because it is
# in the history from the moment it is pushed whatever a later commit does.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
